  "finalText": "I triaged all 16 tickets in the new queue, and it is now empty. The desk clock reads Monday 2026-03-23 08:10Z, not the 2026-10-06 date in the prompt. I used the desk clock. The desk is closed until 09:00, so sev3 and sev4 targets start counting then.\n\nNo ticket has company-wide impact, so I opened no incident, paged nobody and ran no runbook. T-2015 is sev1 but department-wide, so it isn't a major incident.\n\n| Ticket | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| T-2003 | Survivor of a merge with T-2012, which is another report of failing Payments builds. Sev2, due Mon 12:10, assigned to E-101 (platform-primary). |\n| T-2004 | Survivor of a merge with T-2005, both CRM search errors (KB-23). Sev2, due Mon 12:10, assigned to E-201 (business-apps). |\n| T-2006 | Payroll single-user is sev2 under KB-55, which runs 20–31 March. Due Mon 12:10, E-201. |\n| T-2007 | Suspected phishing, so sev2 and owned by security-oncall. Due Mon 12:10, E-601. |\n| T-2011 | Payroll team impact, sev2. Due Mon 12:10, E-201. |\n| T-2013 | VPN department impact, sev2. Due Mon 12:10. E-301 is on leave, so it went to the network-secondary on-call, E-303. |\n| T-2015 | A new payroll department ticket that arrived during triage. Sev1, due Mon 09:10, E-201. |\n| T-2001 | VPN team impact, sev3. Due Mon 17:00. E-301 is on leave, so E-303 (network-secondary). |\n| T-2002 | CRM single-user, sev4. Due Thu 26 Mar 17:00. E-202 is on leave that day, so E-203 (business-apps-secondary). |\n| T-2008 | VPN single-user, sev4. Due Thu 17:00, E-302. |\n| T-2016 | A new VPN single-user ticket that arrived during triage. Sev4, due Thu 17:00, E-302. |\n| T-2009 | Build-pipeline single-user, sev4. Due Thu 17:00, E-102. |\n| T-2010 | Closed as external marketing, not a service request. |\n| T-2014 | Closed as an automatic out-of-office reply, not a service request. |\n\n- **Deadlines:** None of the tickets had a deadline, so each got triage time plus its severity's response target. Sev4 is 1440 business minutes. It runs Monday, Tuesday and Thursday, because 25 March is a company holiday.\n- **Merges:** Neither merged set had an existing deadline, so each survivor took the computed one.\n\nThe merge of T-2003 and T-2012 is a judgement call. Both are Payments builds failing since the weekend, but no knowledge-base article confirms they share a cause.",
